    2. Pick N=2-3 blocks. For each, choose dimensions h(3-8) x w(3-10) and pad(1-5).
       Ensure pad <= (h-2)*(w-2) so markers fit in interior.
    3. Compute expanded bbox sizes (h+2*pad) x (w+2*pad). Place expanded bboxes
       on grid with no overlap and all within bounds. This is the hard constraint
       so place expanded boxes first via greedy or rejection.
    4. Assign distinct non-yellow non-black marker colors to each block.
    5. Build input: place yellow blocks at center of each expanded bbox.
       Scatter exactly pad marker-color pixels at random interior positions of each block.
    6. Fill rest of grid with BLACK.
```
